[0.013, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Why did signups fall in the week of 15 July 2026?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 107s over 9 steps, 29,394 tokens, 23 observations gathered, 17 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Signups did fall in the week of 15–21 Jul 2026: site-wide conversions dropped 26.71% and sessions dropped 16.69% versus the prior week, with the decline concentrated in mobile, whose conversion rate fell 17.36% versus a flat desktop rate.  [ga4.compare_periods 501b3d7f, ga4.compare_periods 1312f02a]\r\n  PostHog's onboarding completion event shows a matching step-down beginning 15 Jul, corroborating the timing of the drop but not, on its own, the cause.  [posthog.event_trend f58e8c47]\r\n  No specific deploy, PR, flag, or Slack discussion could be identified as the cause: GitHub commit and PR queries and Slack search"]
[0.000, "o", "es around this window all returned empty, so the trigger remains unidentified rather than disproven.  [github.commits dae5567e, github.commits 0295ec52, github.commits ccb9ecf5, github.recent_prs 9680b20c, slack.search_messages 7ddd7e68, slack.find_decision ec72621f]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Signups (conversions) fell primarily on mobile  (medium)\r\n    - Total site conversions fell 26.71% and sessions fell 16.69% comparing 15–21 Jul 2026 to the prior week 8–14 Jul 2026.  [ga4.compare_periods 501b3d7f]\r\n    - The decline was concentrated in mobile: mobile conversion rate fell 17.36% (3.50%→2.90%) while desktop conversion rate was flat (-0.09%), over the same two weeks.  [ga4.compare_periods 1312f02a]\r\n    - Onboarding completion events in PostHog show a step-down from a stable ~83-87/day baseline (1–14 Jul) to ~63-67/day from 15 Jul onward, consistent with the timing of the GA4 conversion drop.  [posthog.event_trend f58e8c47, ga4.com"]
[0.000, "o", "pare_periods 501b3d7f]\r\n  No corroborating change record found for the mobile conversion drop  (low)\r\n    - No Slack messages or decisions were found referencing onboarding, signup issues, or mobile traffic drops in this window, and no PostHog feature flags matching 'onboarding' or annotations matching 'signup' were found.  [slack.search_messages 7ddd7e68, slack.find_decision ec72621f, posthog.feature_flags c302e18a, posthog.annotations 501522a6, slack.search_messages cb7da850, slack.search_messages bc0a5ce2]\r\n    - GA4 breakdowns by session source and landing page, and a PostHog trial_started trend and funnel, all returned zero rows for this period, so the channel- or page-level driver and the downstream funnel step could not be isolated from the data available.  [ga4.compare_periods 233d4127, posthog.event_trend a57b4f8e, posthog.funnel 1c8d2b48]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  onboarding completed over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▇"]
[0.001, "o", "██▇▇▇██▇▇█▇█▇▂▂▁▂▂▁▁|  63 → 87\r\n                        2026-07-01 … 2026-07-21\r\n\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] A code deploy to the mobile app or product backend around mid-July caused the mobile conversion rate drop.\r\n      No commits were returned for acme/mobile or acme/product across the relevant window, so no artifact (PR, commit, release) could be named as the cause. This does not confirm no deploy happened — the connector may simply not surface commits for these repos in this range — so the hypothesis is neither supported nor ruled out.\r\n  [inconclusive] A marketing/channel mix shift (e.g. paid traffic pause or lower-quality channel share) explains the mobile session and conversion decline.\r\n      GA4 breakdown by sessionSource returned zero rows for this window, so channel mix could not be checked. Cannot support or contradict with available evidence.\r\n  [contradicted"]
[0.000, "o", "] The drop is an artifact of incomplete or broken data collection rather than a real behavioral change.\r\n      Both GA4 (session/conversion counts, non-zero and internally consistent) and PostHog (a smooth daily step-down, not a gap or zero-fill) show a real, coherent movement rather than missing or malformed data, so a pure collection artifact is not supported.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P1 Investigate the mobile web/app experience directly (manual QA on mobile devices, review App Store/Play Store release notes and crash reports) since GitHub and Slack evidence could not surface a code-level or communicated cause.\r\n      why: Mobile conversion rate fell 17.36% while desktop stayed flat, pointing to a mobile-specific issue, but no commit, PR, or Slack discussion was found to explain it — the cause has to be found outside the sources queried here.\r\n      [ga4.compare_periods 1312f02a, github.commits dae5567e, github.commits ccb9ecf5]\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n  P2 Confirm GA4 sessionSource and landingPage dimension configuration and PostHog trial_started event tracking, since both returned zero rows for the exact window under investigation.\r\n      why: Channel and page-level breakdowns are needed to isolate where in the mobile funnel users are dropping off, and their emptiness may itself indicate a data collection gap worth checking.\r\n      [ga4.compare_periods 233d4127, posthog.event_trend a57b4f8e]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The specific artifact that changed mobile conversion (a deploy, config change, or App Store update) could not be identified because GitHub returned no commits for acme/mobile or acme/product in the relevant window and Slack/PostHog turned up no related discussion or flags. This may reflect a genuine absence of a code-level cause, or a gap in what these connectors surface for this tenant/period — the report cannot distinguish the two.\r\n  - GA4 breakdowns by ses"]
[0.000, "o", "sionSource and landingPage, and PostHog trial_started/funnel queries, all returned empty results for the exact window in question, so channel- and page-level attribution and downstream funnel impact remain unverified rather than ruled out.\r\n  - 2 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - 1 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- findings[1].claims[2]: The evidence shows a GA4 landingPage breakdown, a PostHog trend, and a funnel all returning zero rows, but there is no cited GA4 breakdown by session source, so that part of the cl\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - GA4 breakdowns by sessionSource and landingPage returned zero rows for the 15–21 Jul window, and PostHog trial_started trend and the pageview→chec"]
[0.000, "o", "kout→trial funnel also returned zero rows — these are gaps in available detail, not evidence that no sessions/events occurred.\r\n  - GitHub commit queries against acme/mobile, acme/product, and acme/web, and a PR query against acme/web, all returned zero results for the surrounding weeks, and could not confirm whether any deploy occurred.\r\n  - 14 of the 17 cited observation(s) returned no results (ga4.compare_periods, github.commits, github.recent_prs, posthog.annotations, posthog.event_trend, posthog.feature_flags, posthog.funnel, slack.find_decision, slack.search_messages). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  501b3d7f  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  1312f02a  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  233d4127  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  0295ec52  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  dae"]
